{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPov3hTe6YMN6Bkrzt4Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Btd1XNMNTzWjnX5g2zCWtd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.ard/work/albertcbrown/ard/01M89HPVKQ5VYKR7SKRW2TV7GF; mkdir -p .ard/357; cat > .ard/357/worker-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nTransient push and fetch failures (GitHub 5xx, network errors, token mint errors) are now classified as `ErrTransient` and retried with exponential backoff in the committer's main, code and init lanes. When the budget runs out the job ends with a retryable `push_transient` cause instead of `ard:executor:failed`.\n\n## Changes\n- gitx: new `ErrTransient`; `classifyTransient` on push stderr and on non-shallow fetch stderr (stale lease, non-fast-forward, ref-not-found and repo-access win first); token errors from the network or a 5xx (`ghinstallation`/`go-github` responses) are wrapped too, unless the caller's context ended. Re-exported in effects.\n- committer: `ErrTransient` (wraps the last cause). The main lane keeps separate rejection and transient counters (5 transient retries, 1s doubling, ±25% jitter, `Config.Backoff` overrides it), logs `committer.retry` with reason `transient` at INFO, and after the re-fetch treats a pushed commit that is already in upstream as success (no second commit). `pushNew` does the same for branch-creating pushes (code create, init): it fetches the branch and succeeds if it holds the pushed commit, otherwise keeps `ErrBranchExists`/`ErrInitExists`.\n- closeout: new `CausePushTransient`; a commit failing with `committer.ErrTransient` gives a retry plan. worker: `CommitCode` transient exhaustion finishes with that cause.\n- Tests: gitx classification, token and fetch cases; committer retry, landed push, exhaustion, independent counters, cancelled backoff, jitter, code and init lanes; closeout retry plan.\n\n## Testing\n`go test` for gitx, committer, closeout, worker, effects and reaper: all pass; `go vet ./internal/...` and gofmt are clean. Shallow fetch is deliberately not classified as transient, because existing tests and callers expect network errors there to stay unclassified.\n\n## Open issues\n- The closeout `Job` has no retry-of field, so a close-out commit failure always hands off to retry; the state store still decides whether a second automatic retry happens (not verified in this change).\n- GH006 is not handled, as the plan says (separate issue).\n- The lane holds its semaphore during backoff (up to about a minute).\n- Credential redaction is unchanged (text comes from `g.run`, already scrubbed); no new test for it.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":71672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":871},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0a93f1c-6080-4bb1-a8b4-d8990a60314f","uuid":"6254eb96-20b4-4e58-8af2-3c8104d8fb18","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:32:45.170Z","request_id":"req_011ChPov3Z1zqnPiy6zBgnxA"}
