{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPova4KmufxbQGqMkZoH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Transient push and fetch failures are now retried with backoff, and a failure that outlasts the budget ends with a retryable `push_transient` cause instead of `ard:executor:failed`. Tests pass for gitx, committer, closeout, worker, effects and reaper, `go vet ./internal/...` is clean, and `gofmt -l` flagged nothing in the packages I touched. I did not run the full `go test ./...`.\n\n- **gitx:** a new `ErrTransient` covers 5xx, DNS, connection-reset, timeout and early-EOF errors in push and fetch stderr. It also covers token mint errors from the network or a 5xx, unless the caller's own context ended. Stale lease, non-fast-forward, ref-not-found and repo-access errors are checked first, so their handling is unchanged.\n- **Main lane:** it keeps separate counters for rejections and transient failures. Transient retries use 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s and 16s with ±25% jitter and log `committer.retry` with reason `transient` at INFO. After the re-fetch, a pushed commit already in upstream counts as success with no second commit.\n- **Code-create and init lanes:** after a transient failure they fetch the branch and succeed if it holds the pushed commit; otherwise they keep `ErrBranchExists` or `ErrInitExists`.\n- **Close-out:** a commit failing with `committer.ErrTransient` gives a retry plan, and the worker's `CommitCode` path finishes with the same cause.\n- **Shallow fetch is not classified as transient.** Existing tests expect network errors there to stay unclassified, so only `FetchRef` is.\n- **A close-out commit failure always hands off to retry.** The close-out `Job` has no retry-of field, so I could not apply the \"job is not itself a retry\" rule there. I did not check whether the state store limits a second automatic retry.\n- **GH006 is not handled**, as the plan says; it should be a separate issue.\n- **No new redaction test.** Credential redaction is unchanged because error text still comes from the already-scrubbed push output.\n- **Lane semaphore held during backoff.** It stays held for up to about a minute.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/357/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_read_input_tokens":72543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025},"output_tokens":723,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0a93f1c-6080-4bb1-a8b4-d8990a60314f","uuid":"34a8bf6b-08a7-4d9a-9984-a400a362e5da","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:32:50.367Z","request_id":"req_011ChPovZtuK46jURBLCXErJ"}
